Working equipment: computer provided;
Flexibility: provide flexible scheduling options to accommodate the intern's educational commitments or other obligations;
Professional development: Exposure to various aspects of HR, including internal communication, engagement activities, and learning and development;
Mentoring: provide regular feedback, guidance and on-the-job training from the supervisor and HR Manager;
Networking: participate in company events (both internal and external) and connect with other employees, which can help build a professional network;
Recognition: Recognize the intern's contributions and achievements with a certificate of completion or letter of recommendation.

